    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Parse Reply\nGrammar (case-insensitive): `^(\\d)(?:\\s*(?:start|end)\\s*([+-]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*s?\\s*(earlier|later)?)*$|^reject all$`\nExamples: `2` · `2 start 5s earlier` · `2 end 3s later` · `1 start 2s later end 4s later` · `reject all`.\nOffsets are applied to the chosen candidate's start/end and clamped to `[0, duration]`. `reject all` → Telegram notice → end. Unparseable → Telegram notice → end (nothing rendered).",
        "height": 190,
        "width": 900,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "de0ee2e8-1025-4b77-8ada-c3e0410a5a65",
      "name": "Note 27",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4200,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Implements the CONTRACT.md reply grammar.\nconst review = $('Build Review Message').first().json;\nconst cfg = $('Config').first().json;\nconst raw = String(($input.first().json.data || {}).text || '').trim();\nconst text = raw.toLowerCase().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ');\nconst duration = Number(review.duration_sec) || 0;\n\nconst GRAMMAR = /^(\\d)(?:\\s*(?:start|end)\\s*([+-]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*s?\\s*(earlier|later)?)*$|^reject all$/i;\n\nconst base = { reply: raw, job_id: review.job_id, job_dir: review.job_dir, input: review.input,\n               original: review.original, candidates: review.candidates };\n\nif (text === 'reject all') return [{ json: { ...base, action: 'reject' } }];\nif (!GRAMMAR.test(text)) return [{ json: { ...base, action: 'invalid', error: `Could not parse reply \"${raw}\"` } }];\n\nconst rank = Number(text.match(/^(\\d)/)[1]);\nconst cand = (review.candidates || []).find(c => Number(c.rank) === rank);\nif (!cand) return [{ json: { ...base, action: 'invalid', error: `No candidate #${rank}` } }];\n\nlet start = Number(cand.start), end = Number(cand.end);\nconst clauseRe = /(start|end)\\s*([+-]?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*s?\\s*(earlier|later)?/g;\nlet m;\nwhile ((m = clauseRe.exec(text)) !== null) {\n  const which = m[1];\n  let delta = parseFloat(m[2]);\n  const dir = m[3];\n  if (dir === 'earlier') delta = -Math.abs(delta);\n  else if (dir === 'later') delta = Math.abs(delta);\n  // no direction word: signed number is taken literally (+ = later, - = earlier)\n  if (which === 'start') start += delta; else end += delta;\n}\nconst clamp = v => Math.min(Math.max(0, v), duration || v);\nstart = clamp(start); end = clamp(end);\nif (end <= start) return [{ json: { ...base, action: 'invalid', error: `Window collapsed (start ${start}s ≥ end ${end}s)` } }];\n\nreturn [{ json: { ...base, action: 'render', rank, start: Number(start.toFixed(3)), end: Number(end.toFixed(3)),\n                  duration: Number((end - start).toFixed(3)), candidate: { ...cand, start, end },\n                  captions: cfg.CAPTIONS !== false, offset: cfg.RENDER_OFFSET, audio_mode: cfg.AUDIO_MODE, volume: cfg.VOLUME } }];\n"
      },
